  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "In one of the oldest legends told during the Gu Yue clan Awakening Ceremony, three Gu approach Ren Zu and offer help if he provides for them with his life. He gives his youth to the biggest of the three, and that Gu grants him strength. The same telling later names that Gu the strength Gu, and compares Hope Gu against it as frail and only a tiny ball of light.",
        "chapters": [
          5
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_gu_yue_clan",
          "sys_awakening_ceremony",
          "char_ren_zu",
          "gu_hope_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "With that strength, Ren Zu gains steady food and can fight Predicaments, then learns that strength alone is not enough and must be healed and cultivated rather than spent freely. After he also trades his middle years for wisdom Gu, age catches him. The strength and wisdom Gu say he has nothing left to give, and they leave. Without them he is surrounded again, until Hope Gu takes his heart and drives the Predicaments away.",
        "chapters": [
          5
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "first-deal-and-abandonment",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_wisdom_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A later Ren Zu telling has Rules and Regulation Gu gather many Gu, then leave five when Ren Zu cannot yet subdue the rest. Strength Gu and Wisdom Gu are among those five. Ren Zu offers Strength Gu freedom if it submits. Strength Gu refuses permanent submission, saying it only succumbs to those stronger than him, but offers a new deal: give it his youth again and it will obey for a time. Ren Zu accepts, becomes middle-aged at once, and Strength Gu flies from the net onto his shoulder. He then refuses the matching middle-age deal with Wisdom Gu, and Wisdom Gu tricks him into naming Rules and Regulation so it can escape.",
        "chapters": [
          58
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "second-deal-after-rules-and-regulation",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_rules_and_regulation_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan later reads that choice as the story’s point that strength is the foundation: Ren Zu deals with Strength Gu and gives up wisdom.",
        "chapters": [
          132
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "second-deal-after-rules-and-regulation",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In another stretch of the legend Ren Zu still lists Strength Gu among his companions beside Hope Gu, Rules and Regulation Gu, and Attitude Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          131
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "second-deal-after-rules-and-regulation",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_attitude_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Early tellings mark it as the biggest of the three bargains and as able to land on Ren Zu’s shoulder after the second youth deal.",
        "chapters": [
          5
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-classification-in-the-legends",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "No cited chapter prints a Chinese name or glyph for Strength Gu.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-classification-in-the-legends",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The Legends of Ren Zu describes Immortal Gu under their own names, using wisdom Gu and strength Gu as the examples, while mortal Gu are written more obscurely and need research to identify.",
        "chapters": [
          405
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-classification-in-the-legends",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu",
          "sys_immortal_gu",
          "sys_mortal_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "That line keeps the legendary Strength Gu in the Immortal Gu set named in the book, rather than among the obscure mortal recipes readers must decode.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-classification-in-the-legends",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "When repeated failure Gu costs Ren Zu other companions, Strength Gu also flies out, calls him a failure unworthy of possessing it, and flees. Self Gu from Ren Zu’s heart bites Strength Gu as it flees, taking a piece; Strength Gu shrieks and vanishes like a streak of smoke. Self Gu then tells Ren Zu that from then on he will have his own strength,",
        "chapters": [
          845
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "self-gu-takes-a-bite",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_failure_gu",
          "gu_self_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Later tellings repeat that Self Gu once ate a mouthful of Strength Gu, so Ren Zu has his own strength even when he no longer holds Strength Gu itself.",
        "chapters": [
          1230
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "self-gu-takes-a-bite",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "In Ordinary Abyss, Strength Gu flies from felled trees and tells Boundless Forest Samsara that strength is hidden in the ordinary. It offers great strength for her youth, arguing that waiting decades to finish a ladder would spend that youth anyway. She takes the deal and builds much faster, then grows lazy while a miniman without Strength Gu keeps building until Perseverance Gu forms and he leaves the abyss.",
        "chapters": [
          1276
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "ordinary-abyss-telling",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_ordinary_abyss",
          "char_boundless_forest_samsara",
          "gu_perseverance_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Weighing how to break free of fate, Ren Zu recalls that self Gu once ate a part of strength Gu, and resolves to have it do the same to wisdom Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          2036
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "a-second-bite-planned",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
